    <!-- Quick start -->
    <section class="section fade-up fade-up-3" id="quick-start">
        <h2>1. Quick start</h2>
        <p>Requires <a href="https://bun.sh" target="_blank">Bun</a>. Run this in any terminal:</p>

        <div class="code-inline">
            <code>bun add -g @openparachute/cli &amp;&amp; parachute install vault</code>
        </div>

        <p>What just happened:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>The Parachute CLI is installed globally.</li>
            <li>Parachute Vault is installed and running as a background daemon on <code>127.0.0.1:1940</code> (launchd on macOS, systemd on Linux).</li>
            <li>The Vault MCP is added to your <code>~/.claude.json</code>. Claude Code picks it up on the next session — no restart needed for future sessions.</li>
            <li>An API token is generated and stored locally in <code>~/.claude.json</code> as a Bearer header.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Start a new Claude Code session. Ask it to write a note, query your vault, whatever. The MCP tools <code>create-note</code>, <code>query-notes</code>, <code>update-note</code>, etc. are all available.</p>

        <p>If you ever want to check or restart it: <code>parachute status</code>, <code>parachute restart vault</code>, <code>parachute logs vault</code>.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Claude Chat / ChatGPT / Web -->
    <section class="section" id="claude-chat">
        <h2>2. Use it from Claude, ChatGPT, and the web</h2>
        <p>Claude (web + Desktop + mobile) and ChatGPT (web + Desktop) all connect to external MCPs via their Connectors UI — you paste a public HTTPS URL once and it's available everywhere you use the app. To give them access to your Vault, you need to make your Vault reachable from outside your laptop over HTTPS.</p>

        <p>Two paths, both free. Pick the one that matches what you already have:</p>

        <h3>Path A: Tailscale Funnel (no domain required)</h3>
        <p>If you don't have your own domain, this is the easier path. Tailscale gives you a free <code>*.ts.net</code> URL.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Install <a href="https://tailscale.com/download" target="_blank">Tailscale</a> (free for personal use, 2 minutes) and run <code>tailscale up</code>.</li>
            <li>Enable <a href="https://tailscale.com/kb/1223/funnel" target="_blank">Tailscale Funnel</a> on your tailnet (admin console → Access Controls → add a <code>funnel</code> ACL, and enable HTTPS in DNS settings).</li>
            <li>Run <code>parachute expose public</code>. Your Vault is now at <code>https://&lt;machine&gt;.&lt;tailnet&gt;.ts.net/vault/default</code>.</li>
            <li>Set up an owner password and 2FA on the Vault — required before you expose it publicly:
                <div class="code-inline"><code>parachute vault set-password &amp;&amp; parachute vault 2fa enroll</code></div>
            </li>
            <li>In <a href="https://claude.ai/settings/connectors" target="_blank">claude.ai → Settings → Connectors</a>, click "Add custom connector" and paste your Vault URL. Complete the OAuth handshake.</li>
            <li>For ChatGPT: <a href="https://chatgpt.com" target="_blank">chatgpt.com</a> → Settings → Connectors → same flow.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Path B: Cloudflare Tunnel (if you have a domain)</h3>
        <p>If you already use Cloudflare for DNS on a domain, <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/connections/connect-networks/" target="_blank">Cloudflare Tunnel</a> gives you a stable public URL routed through your own domain.</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Install <code>cloudflared</code>: <code>brew install cloudflared</code> on macOS, or <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/connections/connect-networks/downloads/" target="_blank">see downloads</a>.</li>
            <li><code>cloudflared tunnel login</code>, then create a tunnel: <code>cloudflared tunnel create parachute</code>.</li>
            <li>Route DNS: <code>cloudflared tunnel route dns parachute vault.yourdomain.com</code>.</li>
            <li>Run the tunnel pointing at your local Vault: <code>cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:1940 run parachute</code>.</li>
            <li>Set up owner password + 2FA on the Vault (step 4 above — required before exposing publicly).</li>
            <li>In claude.ai / ChatGPT Connectors, paste <code>https://vault.yourdomain.com/vault/default</code> and complete OAuth.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Quick test (not for production)</h3>
        <p>Cloudflare also has an ephemeral "quick tunnel" that works in 30 seconds without an account: <code>cloudflared tunnel --url http://localhost:1940</code>. The URL is random and expires when you stop the command — good for testing, bad for claude.ai since the URL changes.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Tailnet only -->
    <section class="section" id="tailnet">
        <h2>3. Reach it from your own devices (tailnet-only)</h2>
        <p>If you want your Vault accessible from your phone, tablet, and other devices <em>without</em> exposing it to the public internet, use <a href="https://tailscale.com/kb/1312/serve" target="_blank">Tailscale Serve</a> instead of Funnel:</p>
        <div class="code-inline">
            <code>parachute expose tailnet</code>
        </div>
        <p>Vault is now reachable at <code>https://&lt;machine&gt;.&lt;tailnet&gt;.ts.net/vault/default</code> from any device on your tailnet. External services like claude.ai can't reach it (that's the point) — use this when you only want your own devices talking to the graph.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Beyond your laptop -->
    <section class="section" id="beyond">
        <h2>4. Beyond your laptop</h2>
        <p>Your laptop sleeps. A background daemon is great for real-time use but not ideal if you want your Vault always reachable. Two paths:</p>

        <h3>Wait for Parachute Cloud</h3>
        <p>We're working on a hosted version with the same architecture, same guarantees, no server to run. <a href="https://openparachute.substack.com" target="_blank">Subscribe for updates</a>. Coming in the next few weeks.</p>

        <h3>Run it yourself</h3>
        <p>Parachute Vault is Bun + SQLite. It runs anywhere you can run Bun on a Linux box:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>A small always-on Mac or Raspberry Pi on your network</li>
            <li>A cheap VPS (Render, Railway, Fly.io, Hetzner, DigitalOcean, Vultr)</li>
            <li>A home server you already have</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault/tree/main/deploy" target="_blank">deploy/ directory</a> in the vault repo has a systemd unit for Linux. Install Bun, clone the repo, <code>bun src/cli.ts init</code>, enable the systemd unit. Expose with Cloudflare Tunnel or Caddy + your domain.</p>
        <p>We haven't published step-by-step VPS guides yet — want to see one? <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault/issues" target="_blank">File an issue</a>, and tell us which provider.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Troubleshooting -->
    <section class="section" id="troubleshooting">
        <h2>5. Troubleshooting</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Port 1940 is already in use.</strong> Something else is bound to Vault's default port. Check with <code>lsof -i :1940</code>. Either stop the other process or set <code>PORT=</code> in <code>~/.parachute/vault/.env</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Claude Code doesn't see the MCP.</strong> Start a new Claude Code session — the MCP config is loaded at session start. Run <code>/mcp</code> inside Claude Code to confirm. If missing, check <code>~/.claude.json</code> has a <code>parachute-vault</code> entry with a Bearer token header.</li>
            <li><strong>401 Unauthorized on MCP calls.</strong> Your API token isn't attached. Check the Bearer header in <code>~/.claude.json</code> matches <code>~/.parachute/vault/</code> config output of <code>parachute vault tokens list</code>.</li>
            <li><strong><code>parachute expose public</code> fails with "funnel not enabled".</strong> Go to your <a href="https://login.tailscale.com/admin/acls" target="_blank">Tailscale admin</a> → Access Controls → add a <code>nodeAttrs</code> rule granting <code>funnel</code>. Also enable MagicDNS + HTTPS Certificates under DNS.</li>
            <li><strong>claude.ai OAuth fails with "No pending OAuth flow".</strong> You clicked the home-screen shortcut before completing the handshake. Open the Vault connector URL in a regular tab and restart the OAuth flow.</li>
            <li><strong>Voice memo doesn't transcribe.</strong> Install Scribe: <code>parachute install scribe</code>. Make sure <code>SCRIBE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1943</code> is set in <code>~/.parachute/vault/.env</code>, then <code>parachute restart vault</code>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Found something we missed? <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault/issues" target="_blank">Open an issue</a>.</p>
    </section>

